Subject: [PATCH 01/29] =?UTF-8?q?audio:=20add=20ad=5Forender=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20spatial=20audio=20decoder=20via=20liborender?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an opt-in mpv audio decoder that hands raw access units to
liborender (orender_*), which decodes them via a runtime bridge
plugin and VBAP-renders the spatial objects to N-channel float PCM.
Replaces FFmpeg's downmix path for spatial-capable streams.

- audio/decode/ad_orender.c: the decoder itself (mp_filter shape,
  modeled on ad_spdif.c). Resolves spatial-vs-plain on the first
  packet via orender_is_spatial(); maps orender's per-speaker
  channel labels to mp_chmap; sets PTS from the first decoded
  frame and advances by sample count.
- audio/decode: register in ad_orender.fns, opt-in via `--ad=orender`.
- filters/f_decoder_wrapper.{c,h}: route truehd/eac3 to the orender
  decoder when listed in --ad.
- meson.{build,options}: detect liborender via pkg-config, compile
  ad_orender.c when the `orender` feature is enabled.
- options/options.{c,h}: --ad-orender-{config,bridge-path,osc*}
  surface the renderer's runtime configuration to mpv users.

Reads the shared omniphony config (~/.config/omniphony/config.yaml)
for bridge path, speaker layout and OSC — the same config the orender
CLI and studio use, so a single setup serves all three.
